  1506: - **Two-way sync via git**: the connected git branch is linked to the Lovable project. When you **commit and push** to that branch, Lovable picks up the changes and they appear in the Lovable editor, preview, and any deployed URL.
  1507: - **Frontend hosting**: Lovable builds and serves the React frontend. So your live preview/deployment is the *committed* code — local uncommitted edits on your machine don't reach it until you push.
> 1508: - **The backend is separate**: Lovable only hosts the frontend. Your Laravel API (`backend-laravel/`) runs on your own server (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:8000`), referenced via `VITE_API_BASE_URL`. So a working preview needs both: committed frontend code **and** a running backend the preview can reach.
  1509: - **History protection**: the `AGENTS.md` warns not to rewrite/force-push published history, because Lovable tracks the branch — doing so can break the sync and lose project history.
